407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 318 0 R
/T (Key themes included healthy and stigma-free dialogue about sexuality, menstrual health and sustainability, LGBTQIA+ inclusion, gender justice, democratic engagement, and the use of creative, digital, gamified, and participatory tools in youth work.)
/E (Key themes included healthy and stigma-free dialogue about sexuality, menstrual health and sustainability, LGBTQIA+ inclusion, gender justice, democratic engagement, and the use of creative, digital, gamified, and participatory tools in youth work.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 318 0 R
/T (A central aim of the project was not only to exchange knowledge, but also to create practical educational tools that could be adapted and used in different youth work settings. During the Training Course, participants worked in international groups to design, develop, and test their own workshop concepts. These activities were shaped by their professional experience, local realities, and the needs of the young people they work with.)
/E (A central aim of the project was not only to exchange knowledge, but also to create practical educational tools that could be adapted and used in different youth work settings. During the Training Course, participants worked in international groups to design, develop, and test their own workshop concepts. These activities were shaped by their professional experience, local realities, and the needs of the young people they work with.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
409 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 318 0 R
/T (This document presents the workshops created and tested by participants during the Training Course, together with implementation tips for youth workers, educators, and facilitators who wish to use or adapt them. The toolkit is designed as a practical collection of non-formal education tools that can support sexuality education activities across Europe and beyond.)
/E (This document presents the workshops created and tested by participants during the Training Course, together with implementation tips for youth workers, educators, and facilitators who wish to use or adapt them. The toolkit is designed as a practical collection of non-formal education tools that can support sexuality education activities across Europe and beyond.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 318 0 R
/T (By sharing these methods, the project aims to encourage youth workers to facilitate safer, more inclusive, and more informed conversations around sexuality. It also supports the wider goal of empowering young people to understand their rights, challenge stigma and discrimination, and contribute to more equal, respectful, and democratic communities.)
/E (By sharing these methods, the project aims to encourage youth workers to facilitate safer, more inclusive, and more informed conversations around sexuality. It also supports the wider goal of empowering young people to understand their rights, challenge stigma and discrimination, and contribute to more equal, respectful, and democratic communities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
