/T (This workshop addresses sexual education through the lens of respect, personal boundaries, safety, and open dialogue. It is designed especially for young people coming from conservative backgrounds or contexts where sexuality education may be limited, taboo, or influenced by social, cultural, religious, or political restrictions. The activity can be particularly relevant for young people from countries or communities where open conversations about sexuality, gender, consent, identity, or relationships may be less accessible, including young people from Slavic-speaking contexts, Eastern European backgrounds, or Muslim families arriving in European countries.)
/E (This workshop addresses sexual education through the lens of respect, personal boundaries, safety, and open dialogue. It is designed especially for young people coming from conservative backgrounds or contexts where sexuality education may be limited, taboo, or influenced by social, cultural, religious, or political restrictions. The activity can be particularly relevant for young people from countries or communities where open conversations about sexuality, gender, consent, identity, or relationships may be less accessible, including young people from Slavic-speaking contexts, Eastern European backgrounds, or Muslim families arriving in European countries.)
