872 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 364 0 R
/T (If participants raise questions related to trauma, violence, abuse, coercion, or unsafe situations, facilitators should not try to handle these alone in the group. They should follow safeguarding procedures and refer the young person to appropriate trusted adults, counsellors, protection services, or local support organisations.)
/E (If participants raise questions related to trauma, violence, abuse, coercion, or unsafe situations, facilitators should not try to handle these alone in the group. They should follow safeguarding procedures and refer the young person to appropriate trusted adults, counsellors, protection services, or local support organisations.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
873 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 364 0 R
/T (For a 30-minute version, facilitators should keep the presentation short and focus mainly on anonymous questions and basic concepts. For a 90-minute version, facilitators can include more interactive elements, such as small-group discussions, scenario analysis, role-play, or a myth-busting exercise.)
/E (For a 30-minute version, facilitators should keep the presentation short and focus mainly on anonymous questions and basic concepts. For a 90-minute version, facilitators can include more interactive elements, such as small-group discussions, scenario analysis, role-play, or a myth-busting exercise.)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
